Pattern 2: Level-Wise Processing (Breadth-First Search)
The workhorse of Tree traversals, Graph Shortest-Paths, and Grid explorations.

1. The Concept
To process nodes level by level, record the exact queue size before starting the current level's for loop (int size = q.size()). That snapshot ensures you process only the current level's nodes and do not bleed into the next level's children being added simultaneously.

2. Java Blueprint (Tree Level Order Traversal)
Java


public List<List<Integer>> levelOrder(TreeNode root) {
    List<List<Integer>> result = new ArrayList<>();
    if (root == null) return result;
    
    Queue<TreeNode> queue = new ArrayDeque<>();
    queue.offer(root);
    
    while (!queue.isEmpty()) {
        int levelSize = queue.size(); // CRITICAL: Freeze current level size
        List<Integer> currentLevel = new ArrayList<>();
        
        for (int i = 0; i < levelSize; i++) {
            TreeNode currentNode = queue.poll();
            currentLevel.add(currentNode.val);
            
            // Push children for the NEXT level
            if (currentNode.left != null) queue.offer(currentNode.left);
            if (currentNode.right != null) queue.offer(currentNode.right);
        }
        result.add(currentLevel);
    }
    return result;
}

3. Essential Interview Questions
